<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Sept 23.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Sept 23.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    300.00   1.89</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    277.70   3.86</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 190.72   8.43</p>
<p> 4   Adel Bton Cement     119.57   1.65</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	  117.49   2.15</p>
<p> 6   T N T		    112.23   1.56</p>
<p> 7   Herald Rsc	     101.77   1.15</p>
<p> 8   Forrestania Gold	83.33   2.10</p>
<p> 9   Westral Forest	  73.19   2.02</p>
<p>10   Harris Scarfe	   69.41   1.18</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     2.98   0.72</p>
<p> 2   Computer Power	   3.27   3.35</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		3.55   0.63</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd		5.28   0.62</p>
<p> 5   BTR Plc		    6.02   5.42</p>
<p> 6   McIntosh Sec	     6.43   0.80</p>
<p> 7   Pac Mutal Aust	   6.58   2.35</p>
